  "about": "The thirty-seven gases Table C.2, \"Molecular weights and ratios of specific heats for some commonly used gases\", prints on the last page of Appendix C, after the five pages of Table C.1. Columns as printed: \"Gas or vapour\", \"Molecular weight, M kg/mole\" and \"Ratio of specific heats, gamma\". Every cell is filled, no cell carries a footnote marker, and the page prints no credit of any kind: the five references the appendix gives on printed page 717 are tied by name to Table C.1, and the only sentence about this table says what it is for, \"a table of properties of gases, which is particularly useful for calculating control valve noise\". Saturated steam is the only interval, 1.25 to 1.32, and is held as one. Six cells are not held at all: four molar masses that do not belong to the molecule their row names and two ratios of specific heats outside what the quantity can be. Each carries what the page prints and the argument is in docs/ERRATA.md, which also records why the other thirty-one rows with a formula mass are what makes those six a defect rather than a convention.",
